           <p>My guided tour of the Opera House interior cost $43, and I would pay it twice over. Our guide showed us the Concert Hall with its soaring ceiling and the 10,000-pipe grand organ, and I listened as she explained how the acoustics were designed to make every seat feel close to the performers. The taste of the flat white I grabbed from the Opera Bar afterward — rich, smooth, perfectly bitter — became my official flavour of Sydney. I sat on the terrace with the harbour stretching out before me and watched ferries crisscross the water like slow green beetles, their wakes spreading in white V-shapes behind them. However, the real surprise was the Manly Ferry. For just $10 return fare, I had a thirty-minute harbour cruise that passed under the Bridge and alongside the Opera House, with views that rivalled any $200 dinner cruise. The wind off the harbour was cool and bracing, and I stood on the open deck at the stern and watched the city skyline shrink behind me, feeling the salt spray on my arms.</p>
 
